---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
const updated = 'September 25, 2026';
---
<Page title="Privacy Policy" description="How BlenderHacks handles your information.">
  <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>
  <p>This policy explains what information {SITE.name} ({SITE.url}) collects and how it's used.</p>
  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>We don't ask you to create an account and we don't collect names or email addresses unless you choose to email us. Like most websites, our hosting provider may automatically log basic technical data (such as IP address, browser type, and pages requested) to keep the site running and secure.</p>
  <h2>Cookies and affiliate links</h2>
  <p>This site itself does not set tracking cookies. When you click an affiliate link (for example, to Amazon), the destination site may set cookies so it can credit us for any qualifying purchase. Those cookies are governed by that site's own privacy policy, such as <a href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/help/customer/display.html?nodeId=GX7NJQ4ZB8MHFRNJ" rel="noopener">Amazon's Privacy Notice</a>.</p>
  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>We don't currently use analytics. If we add them, we'll update this page to say which service we use and what it collects.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
</Page>
